    {
      "name": "windows-qt6-base",
      "displayName": "Windows Qt 6.12 (Ninja, vcpkg-free)",
      "description": "Regression baseline for the Qt6 route that docs-qt5-downgrade-plan.md measures every mechanical rewrite against. This is the Qt6 twin of windows-qt5-base: same Ninja generator, same 'no toolchainFile' stance, same vcvars64-injected invocation (run with .workbuddy/run-vcvars.py, see .workbuddy/qt5-port/run-qt6-smoke.sh), and the same location-independent MSVC discovery, so a Qt5-vs-Qt6 diff is a pure source diff rather than a generator/toolchain diff. The kit is the stock Qt 6.12.0 win64_msvc2022_64 prebuilt tree installed at C:/Qt/6.12.0/msvc2022_64 (.workbuddy/qt5-port/install-qt6.py); the audited version is still pinned by scripts/qt-toolchain.json and asserted by snow_find_qt() with find_package(... EXACT), so pointing this at a different patch release fails loudly at configure time instead of silently drifting.",
